WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.689
Business day eleven. The account was open, but the client's services were not all ready.

2
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.669
Teams can track their own tasks.

3
00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:15.876
The customer's onboarding crosses those team boundaries.

4
00:00:15.976 --> 00:00:17.760
RE-ViVE connects that view.

5
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.481
Here is Business Account Setup, one service workflow within business onboarding.

6
00:00:22.581 --> 00:00:26.093
Thirteen thousand requests, seventy-five different paths.

7
00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:28.873
About a quarter follow the reported standard path,

8
00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:31.397
and the average request takes thirteen days.

9
00:00:31.677 --> 00:00:34.677
Drill down from an Overview chart to the process map,

10
00:00:34.777 --> 00:00:38.183
with that selection carried through. Here, Hospitality.

11
00:00:38.663 --> 00:00:43.839
Back across account setup, examine documents received and AML approval.

12
00:00:43.939 --> 00:00:50.544
About six days on average at this activity. Elapsed duration is not necessarily idle time.

13
00:00:52.624 --> 00:00:55.048
Right-click the step to open Influencers,

14
00:00:55.148 --> 00:00:58.724
and break down associated requests by city or segment.

15
00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:01.888
These differences help focus the investigation.

16
00:01:01.988 --> 00:01:04.049
Compare two groups side by side.

17
00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:08.899
Here, the e-signature step takes start-ups about half the time it takes SMEs.

18
00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:13.193
Compare segments or time periods, alongside your global filters.

19
00:01:13.293 --> 00:01:17.061
Drill down to the underlying request and its recorded events.

20
00:01:17.161 --> 00:01:19.457
This request took five and a half days.

21
00:01:19.557 --> 00:01:24.797
Its AML approval activity was recorded five times across three days.

22
00:01:24.897 --> 00:01:28.836
A pattern to investigate with the team, with the evidence in hand.

23
00:01:28.936 --> 00:01:32.832
Account setup is one service workflow within business onboarding.

24
00:01:32.932 --> 00:01:38.236
The same foundation maps other service workflows, including EFT processing,

25
00:01:38.336 --> 00:01:41.592
using connected records from the systems involved.

26
00:01:41.692 --> 00:01:44.287
Without drawing each workflow map by hand.

27
00:01:44.387 --> 00:01:48.837
As connected records change, the maps reflect how work actually runs.

28
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:51.307
RE-ViVE shows where to investigate,

29
00:01:51.407 --> 00:01:55.729
with evidence to explore why, so your teams can decide what to change.

30
00:01:55.829 --> 00:01:59.277
Request a banking walkthrough to discuss your own workflows,

31
00:01:59.377 --> 00:02:02.719
and see how to trace where a business request spends its time.